<title>JAPAN: JR West seen issuing Y55 bln of straights--sources.</title>
<headline>JR West seen issuing Y55 bln of straights--sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Japan Railway Co (JR West) is expected to set terms soon on 55 billion yen of domestic straight bonds, underwriting sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The decision on the terms could be made on Tuesday, the sources said.</p>
<p>They said the company would likely issue 25 billion yen of 10-year bonds and 30 billion yen of 20-year bonds.</p>
<p>A JR West spokesman declined to comment.</p>
</text>
